# MorphoMesh: AI 3D Creature Generation Pipeline & FastMCP Blender Bridge

[![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-0.1.0-blue.svg)](pyproject.toml)
[![Protocol](https://img.shields.io/badge/protocol-FastMCP%201.28.1-green.svg)](docs/MCP_SPECIFICATION.md)
[![Blender](https://img.shields.io/badge/Blender-5.2.1%20LTS-orange.svg)](https://www.blender.org)
[![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-macOS%20Apple%20Silicon%20|%20Linux%20x86__64-purple.svg)](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache--2.0-lightgrey.svg)](LICENSE)

**MorphoMesh** is an automated, AI-driven 3D creature and animal generation pipeline and Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that connects **Google Antigravity 2.0** with **Blender 5.2.1 LTS**. Purpose-built for non-humanoid anatomical synthesis, MorphoMesh solves the acute geometric, topological, and biomechanical challenges of generating realistic quadrupeds (canines, felines, equines), avians (raptors, birds), and multi-limbed, winged fantasy chimeras (dragons, griffins) directly from text prompts into fully rigged, textured, and render-ready Blender scenes.

